course: dictionary
lesson: 14260
title: A word from the mountains: névé
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one subject, like science or geography. You may never have met névé before, but the words around it can help. «On the high mountain, the snow was old and grainy, not soft and white like new snow.» Old, grainy snow is the clue here.
explain: Névé is a noun, and it is usually uncountable, so we say «some névé» rather than «two névés». It comes from French, which is why you may see the accent, névé, in English books. Without the accent, the word is spelled neve.
explain: Be careful with look-alikes. Neve is not never or nerve, even though they look similar. If a sentence is about snow on a mountain, check the meaning that fits the snow.
fact: Névé means old, grainy snow on a glacier or high mountain.
fact: Névé has partly melted and refrozen, so it is no longer soft new snow.
fact: The order goes fresh snow, then névé, then glacier ice.
fact: Névé is also called firn in some books.
fact: «Névé» is not the same as «never» or «nerve», even though the spelling is close.
exercise: «The snow on the high slope was old and grainy.» What is this kind of snow called? | *Névé | Fresh powder | Nerve | Never
exercise: «The névé slowly packed down and turned into glacier ice.» What does névé turn into? | Sand | Fresh snow | Rain | *Glacier ice
exercise: Where is névé found? | At sea level in a warm town | In a desert | In a city park | *On a glacier or high mountain
test: Put these in the right order, from the start to the end. | Glacier ice, névé, fresh snow | Glacier ice, fresh snow, névé | *Fresh snow, névé, glacier ice | Névé, glacier ice, fresh snow
test: Ella writes «The mountain was covered in neve.» Her teacher says it should be névé. What does névé mean? | A cold wind on a hill | Never or nerve | *Old, grainy snow on a glacier, partly melted and refrozen | A type of rock
exam: «Walkers crossed the névé carefully.» What is the best meaning of névé here? | A small river | *Old, grainy snow on a glacier | Hot sand | Fresh rain
